\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\cf1\ul\f0\fs32\lang9 NGINX CONFIGURATION TO RUN MULTIPLE APPLICATION \par
\par
\cf0\ulnone Navigate to project directory,run the build command\par
\cf1 sudo npm run build\par
\cf0 copy the build files to a directory like /var/www/html or a custom path under /var/www/ depending on configuration\par
\cf1 sudo cp -r /ems-practice/build/* /var/www/ems/\par
sudo cp -r /arzoo1/build/* /var/www/arzoo/\par
\par
\cf0 custom directory for applications\par
\cf1 sudo mkdir -p /var/www/ems\par
sudo mkdir -p /var/www/arzoo\par
\cf0 After copying files\cf1\par
\ul\par
\cf0\ulnone To configure nginx to run both the ems application the arzoo application,we need to setup server blocks(virtual hosts) for each application.\par
\cf2 Server blocks, often referred to as virtual hosts in Nginx, allow you to host multiple applications or websites on a single server using different domain names or IP addresses. Each server block defines how requests for a particular domain or subdomain should be handled.\par
\cf0\fs24 Key Components of Server Blocks\cf2\par
\cf0 Listen Directive\cf2 :Specifies the port on which the server should listen (usually port 80 for HTTP and 443 for HTTPS).\par
\cf0 Server Name\cf2 :Defines the domain name(s) or subdomain(s) that the server block responds to.\par
\cf0 Location Block\cf2 :Defines how to handle requests to specific paths. You can specify routing, proxying, or serve static files.\par
\cf0 Proxy Pass\cf2 :Used to forward requests to another server or service, such as a backend application running on a different port\fs32 .\par
\par
\cf1\ul\b Nginx configuration of ems application\par
\cf0\ulnone\b0 1----\ul first create configuration file\par
\ulnone /etc/nginx/site-available/\cf1 emsappl\par
server \{\par
    listen 80;\par
    server_name 192.168.36.10; # Replace with your domain or IP if necessary\par
    root /var/www/ems;\par
    index index.html;\par
    location / \{\par
        try_files $uri /index.html;\par
    \}\par
\}\par
\par
\cf0 2----\ul enable the configuration\par
\ulnone for this create a symlink in \cf3 site-enabled\par
\cf1 sudo ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/ems  /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/\par
\par
\cf0 3----\ul test the configuration\ulnone\par
for this run the command\par
\cf1 sudo nginx -t\par
\par
\cf0 4--\ul Restart the nginx\ulnone\par
\cf1 sudo systemctl restart nginx\par

